{{!-- Cover fields injected into the NATIVE Wall configuration sheet (cover.js Unit 3).
      Inputs are named flags.<scope>.* so the sheet's own form submit persists them.

      ⚠ THE BOOK TAG IS ITS OWN SPAN, and that is a LAYOUT decision, not decoration. Core gives a
      `.form-group label` `flex: 1 1 0%`, which on this 480px sheet is 133px — rig-measured, a
      34-character label wrapped to THREE lines and grew the row to 96px. Splitting the tag out lets
      it sit on a designed second line at a smaller weight instead of breaking mid-phrase. The label's
      textContent is unchanged ("Cover SP (Core p.103)"), so the keeper reads the same string.

      ⭐ EVERY FIELD AND BUTTON CARRIES ITS BOOK (user ruling 2026-08-26): a SHORT book-tagged label
      so a GM can see at a glance which rulebook a number comes from, and a `data-tooltip` written in
      plain language saying what the field does mechanically, where it comes from, and — the part
      that actually matters under the structure-as-opt-in design — WHAT LEAVING IT BLANK MEANS.
      The labels stay short on purpose; the teaching lives in the tooltip.

      ⭐ THE TWO MODELS, which is what the hint block exists to explain:
        SP alone            → Core p.103 cover. Soaks, permanent, no cards.
        SP + a structure    → Maximum Metal p.58. Chews, destroys, breaches, repairs.
      Structure is PREFILLED at 3 × SP by the SP handler in cover.js, visibly, so opting in is one
      keystroke and opting out (clear the field) is one keystroke.

      ⭐ THE PROSE MOVED ONTO HOVER (user ruling 2026-08-27, the pre-ship walk: the block "eats half the
      screen"). Four paragraphs of teaching used to stand open above the fields — rig-measured at 4 stacked
      `.hint` blocks on a 480px sheet, which is most of a native Wall config before a single number is
      reachable. Each is now a ONE-LINE summary carrying the SAME full text as its `data-tooltip`, so the
      words are not lost, they are asked for: nothing was deleted from `lang/en.json` and the long strings
      are still the single source for what each rule says.
      ⛔ THE BOOK NAMES STAY ON THE FACE, not in the tooltip. "Core p.103" and "Maximum Metal p.58" are what
      a GM scans for to know which rulebook a number comes from (the 2026-08-26 ruling), so the mode line
      prints both in the open and every field label keeps its own book tag beside it.
      ⚠ The BREACHED note is NOT a hint and does not collapse: it is a statement about this wall's current
      state, and a state notice a reader has to hover to discover is a state notice nobody reads.

      i18n via CPLocal throughout; no inline styles, no strings built in JS. --}}
<fieldset class="cp-cover-wall-fields">
    <legend>{{CPLocal "CoverWallLegend"}}</legend>
    {{!-- The info glyph on each line IS the hover affordance — a one-line summary with no signal that
          more exists reads as all there is. One glyph per line, not one for the block, because each
          line carries a DIFFERENT rule behind it. --}}
    <div class="cp-cover-wall-hints">
        <p class="hint cp-cover-hint" data-tooltip="{{#if isDoor}}{{CPLocal 'CoverWallDoorHint'}}{{else}}{{CPLocal 'CoverWallHint'}}{{/if}}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
            <span>{{#if isDoor}}{{CPLocal "CoverWallDoorHintShort"}}{{else}}{{CPLocal "CoverWallHintShort"}}{{/if}}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="hint cp-cover-hint" data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallModeHint'}}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
            <span>{{CPLocal "CoverWallModeHintShort"}}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="hint cp-cover-hint" data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallLowCoverHint'}}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
            <span>{{CPLocal "CoverWallLowCoverHintShort"}}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="hint cp-cover-hint" data-tooltip="{{#if isDoor}}{{CPLocal 'CoverWallDoorBreachHint'}}{{else}}{{CPLocal 'CoverWallBreachHint'}}{{/if}}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info"></i>
            <span>{{#if isDoor}}{{CPLocal "CoverWallDoorBreachHintShort"}}{{else}}{{CPLocal "CoverWallBreachHintShort"}}{{/if}}</span>
        </p>
    </div>
    {{#if breached}}
    <p class="hint cp-cover-breached-note">{{CPLocal "CoverWallBreachedNote"}}</p>
    {{/if}}
    <div class="form-group">
        <label data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallSPTip'}}">{{CPLocal "CoverWallSPName"}} <span class="cp-cover-book">{{CPLocal "CoverWallSPBook"}}</span></label>
        <div class="form-fields">
            <input type="number" name="flags.{{scope}}.coverSp" value="{{sp}}" min="0" step="1"
                   data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallSPTip'}}"/>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="form-group">
        <label data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallPoolTip'}}">{{CPLocal "CoverWallPoolName"}} <span class="cp-cover-book">{{CPLocal "CoverWallPoolBook"}}</span></label>
        <div class="form-fields">
            <input type="number" name="flags.{{scope}}.coverPool" value="{{pool}}" min="0" step="1"
                   data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallPoolTip'}}"/>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="form-group">
        <label data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallPoolMaxTip'}}">{{CPLocal "CoverWallPoolMaxName"}} <span class="cp-cover-book">{{CPLocal "CoverWallPoolMaxBook"}}</span></label>
        <div class="form-fields">
            <input type="number" name="flags.{{scope}}.coverPoolMax" value="{{poolMax}}" min="0" step="1"
                   data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallPoolMaxTip'}}"/>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="form-group cp-cover-wall-buttons">
        <button type="button" class="cp-cover-wall-clear" data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverWallClearTip'}}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-eraser"></i> {{CPLocal "CoverWallClearBtn"}}
        </button>
        {{#if breached}}
        <button type="button" class="cp-cover-wall-repair" data-tooltip="{{CPLocal 'CoverRepairTip'}}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-trowel-bricks"></i> {{CPLocal "CoverRepairBtn"}}
        </button>
        {{/if}}
    </div>
    {{!-- A free-text material/name field lived here. It was removed: the three structure numbers
          are the whole of what a cover wall needs, and the name added a field to fill in for no
          mechanical effect. Values already stored on existing walls are still READ for the wall's
          display name (cover.js coverWallsOn) — nothing writes the flag any more. --}}
</fieldset>
